# [[Bylaws#Notice must be given to the Directors at least 30 calendar days before the Board of Directors may consider an amendment, supplement, or repeal of the Charter or these Bylaws.|§3.2.2]] — Notice must be given to the Directors at least 30 calendar days before the Board of Directors may consider an amendment, supplement, or repeal of the Charter or these Bylaws.
#* {{Font color|blue|It appears this means the Board needs 30 notice before we can decide to amend the bylaws.  Propose to reduce this to 7 or 14 days.}}
#* [[Bylaws#Waiver of Notice|§3.5]] — {{Font color|blue|May be a way for a Board of Directors meeting to bypass the notice.}}
# [[Bylaws#Notice must be given to the Ordinary Members at least 30 calendar days before the Annual Meeting of Members or a Special Meeting of Members may consider an amendment, supplement, or repeal of the Charter or these Bylaws.|§3.2.3]] — Notice must be given to the Ordinary Members at least 30 calendar days before the Annual Meeting of Members or a Special Meeting of Members may consider an amendment, supplement, or repeal of the Charter or these Bylaws.
#* {{Font color|blue|It appears this means the Ordinary Members needs 30 notice before we can decide to amend the bylaws.  Propose to reduce this to 7 or 14 days.}}
#* [[Bylaws#Waiver of Notice|§3.5]] — {{Font color|blue|May be a way for a Board of Directors meeting to bypass the notice.}}
# [[Bylaws#An Ordinary Member must submit an application for membership via mwstake.org.|§4.3.1.2]] — An Ordinary Member must submit an application for membership via mwstake.org.
#* {{Font color|blue|We should add an application link to mwstake.org.}}
# [[Bylaws#The Board of Directors or its designate must approve the application of an Ordinary Member.|§4.3.1.6]] — The Board of Directors or its designate must approve the application of an Ordinary Member.
#* {{Font color|blue|Just a note, currently we'd need approval from the Board for every new Ordinary Member.  I suppose this could just be a circulated email.}}
# [[Bylaws#Notice of the date, time, and place of the Annual Meeting of Members and Special Meetings of Members must be given to all Directors, Ordinary Members, and Corporate Members at least thirty calendar days prior to the date of the meeting.|§4.6.4]] — Notice of the date, time, and place of the Annual Meeting of Members and Special Meetings of Members must be given to all Directors, Ordinary Members, and Corporate Members at least thirty calendar days prior to the date of the meeting.
#* {{Font color|blue|Propose to reduce this to 7 or 14/15 days.}}
#* {{Font color|blue|We should amend the bylaws to enclose all numeric days in parentheses, for example "(30) days".  Additionally, numbers should be the same, for example "at least eighteen (18) years of age".}}
#* {{Font color|blue|Not related, but all references to mwstake.org should be a link to the main page.}}

==MWStake Meeting==
Steps to create a new MWStake meeting:
# Sign into MWStake (if you don't have an account, contact Mark)
# On the sidebar, click the calendar icon with the "+"
# Select the Start/Stop Date/Time
#* {{Note|Currently the date picker isn't working on this site, but Mark has an [[Action:4|action to fix it]].  It should be in the form: <code>2019/09/06</code> }}
#* {{Note|Traditionally we've been meeting at 15:30 UTC}}
# Enter the meeting URL
#* {{Note|Currently we're using Bryan's Google Hangout which can handle up to 25 attendees: <code><nowiki>https://meet.google.com/mdd-ufhn-ksb</nowiki></code>}}
# Add a "Meeting Agenda" header, see [[Event:92|any previous meeting for format]] (this could be built into the Event template)
# Add the Etherpad link under a new "Notes" header (this could be built into the Event template)
#* {{Note|The URL for the Etherpad link can just be updated to reflect the meeting date, e.g. <code><nowiki>https://etherpad.wikimedia.org/p/mwstake-2019-10</nowiki></code>}}
# Add an "Action board" header with the following (this could be built into the Event template):
#: <SyntaxHighlight lang="linux-config">
{{Actionable board
