==Notes== Shared notes: https://etherpad.wikimedia.org/p/mwstake-2019-10
# {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} '''Process & Safety Management (PSM) with MW + SMW''' #* I developed a Hazard & Risk analysis for PSM to meet ISO & OSHA requirements using MediaWiki + Semantic MediaWiki #* {{Action}} {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} should plan a presentation of this for the [[Event:95|next mwstake meeting]]. # {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} '''Announcing SMWCon2020''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} During SMWCon2019, Matteo Busanelli announced his desire to chair SMWCon 2020 #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} MWStake should support the conference #* {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} 3rd party MW Maintainers "hang out" at SMWCons #* {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} MWStake should definitely support SMWCon & EMWCon, but what does "support" mean? So far, we haven't been able to support financially, we might be able to in the future, but unsure now. #* {{Agenda presenter|Bernard}} There is potential for financial support by [https://www.opensemanticdata.org/ OSDA] #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} As a note, OSDA wasn't able to support SMWCon 2019
==Action board== {{Actionable board |Open |Event:93 |Extension, Conference |True |View |{{PAGENAME}} }}

{{Event |mwstake-meeting=Yes |start-date=2019/10/04 |start-hour=15 |start-minute=30 |end-date=2019/10/04 |end-hour=16 |end-minute=30 |url=https://meet.google.com/mdd-ufhn-ksb |attendees=Bryan Hildebrand, Mark Hershberger, Cindy Cicalese, Bernard Krabina, Brian Wolf, Gergo, Lex Sulzer, Markus Glaser, Rich Evans, Richard Heigl, Vincent Brooks, Sabine Melnicki, Greg Rundlett }} ==Meeting agenda== # '''Wait for attendees & chat''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} # <del>'''Wiki Quickie''' {{Agenda time|10 min}}</del> - No topic # '''Consider MWStake role/support for SMWCon Fall 2020''' {{Agenda time|10 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} # '''Sunflower distribution''' {{Agenda time|20 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} # '''MediaWiki news channel''' {{Agenda time|15 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Richard}}
==Notes== Shared notes: https://etherpad.wikimedia.org/p/mwstake-2019-10
# '''Process & Safety Management (PSM) with MW + SMW''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} I developed a Hazard & Risk analysis for PSM to meet ISO & OSHA requirements using MediaWiki + Semantic MediaWiki #* {{Action}} {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} should plan a presentation of this for the [[Event:95|next mwstake meeting]]. # '''Announcing SMWCon 2020''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} During SMWCon2019, Matteo Busanelli announced his desire to chair SMWCon 2020 #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} MWStake should support the conference #* {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} 3rd party MW Maintainers "hang out" at SMWCons #* {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} MWStake should definitely support SMWCon & EMWCon, but what does "support" mean? So far, we haven't been able to support financially, we might be able to in the future, but unsure now. #* {{Agenda presenter|Bernard}} There is potential for financial support by [https://www.opensemanticdata.org/ OSDA] #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} As a note, OSDA wasn't able to support SMWCon 2019 # '''Announcing EMWCon 2020''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} I have full support of my management #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Would like to determine an organizing committee. Who is in-charge of the process? #* {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} We should define the process (it doesn't currently exist), but we would like to help where we can #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Noted, I just don't want to do anything out of normal practices #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Gave some background on NASA with regards to the conference and a possible tour #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} NASA is spread into 10 field centers #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} NASA Glen in Cleveland Ohio is lesser known. Most others are "mission" oriented, further north facilities are "tech/research" divisions #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} NASA Plum Brook Station is located in rural Ohio, "we are a torture chamber for equipment that is launched". Others design equipment, we reproduce flight/operation conditions #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We could do a tour including the world's largest space vacuum chamber #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We can offer conference facilities at no cost #** {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Are Foreign Nationals OK? #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Great question. We can either host within NASA, but would need prior notice for admitting foreign nationals or host at the [https://www.kalaharimeetings.com/ohio Kalahari conference center] (literally across the street) which would not need any prior notice. What are we trying to prioritize? 1) Cost or 2) Non-US attendance? #** {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} We have the budget from when we hosted in Virginia @ MITRE and we had foreign nationals which came with some restrictions, but we were able to accommodate #** {{Agenda presenter|Brian}} If the location requires early foreign national registration, it should be advertised early & clearly #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We would need to know the Min/Max attendees to contact Kalahari, do we know that? #** {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Min/Max is probably around 30-80, but it probably won't exceed 50 #** {{Agenda presenter|Gergo}} If you advertise the tour of NASA, we could get 100+ attendees, some of which have never used MW :) #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We should try to optimize "Maximum Pull", try to get the most people able to come. In Paris, 2 people added in the last 24 hours #** {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} Europeans will likely need to plan in advance anyway to just make the flight, usually 4 weeks #** {{Agenda presenter|Brian}} As a Canadian, we book at least 4 weeks due to cost. Also, Early access to program content is always a good idea
==Action board== {{Actionable board |Open |Event:93 |Extension, Conference |True |View |{{PAGENAME}} }}

{{Event |mwstake-meeting=Yes |start-date=2019/10/04 |start-hour=15 |start-minute=30 |end-date=2019/10/04 |end-hour=16 |end-minute=30 |url=https://meet.google.com/mdd-ufhn-ksb |attendees=Bryan Hildebrand, Mark Hershberger, Cindy Cicalese, Bernard Krabina, Brian Wolf, Gergo, Lex Sulzer, Markus Glaser, Rich Evans, Richard Heigl, Vincent Brooks, Sabine Melnicki, Greg Rundlett }} ==Meeting agenda== # '''Wait for attendees & chat''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} # <del>'''Wiki Quickie''' {{Agenda time|10 min}}</del> - No topic # '''Consider MWStake role/support for SMWCon Fall 2020''' {{Agenda time|10 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} # '''Sunflower distribution''' {{Agenda time|20 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} # '''MediaWiki news channel''' {{Agenda time|15 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Richard}}
==Notes== Shared notes: https://etherpad.wikimedia.org/p/mwstake-2019-10
# '''Process & Safety Management (PSM) with MW + SMW''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} I developed a Hazard & Risk analysis for PSM to meet ISO & OSHA requirements using MediaWiki + Semantic MediaWiki #* {{Action}} {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} should plan a presentation of this for the [[Event:95|next mwstake meeting]]. # '''Announcing SMWCon 2020''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} During SMWCon2019, Matteo Busanelli announced his desire to chair SMWCon 2020 #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} MWStake should support the conference #* {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} 3rd party MW Maintainers "hang out" at SMWCons #* {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} MWStake should definitely support SMWCon & EMWCon, but what does "support" mean? So far, we haven't been able to support financially, we might be able to in the future, but unsure now. #* {{Agenda presenter|Bernard}} There is potential for financial support by [https://www.opensemanticdata.org/ OSDA] #* {{Agenda presenter|Lex}} As a note, OSDA wasn't able to support SMWCon 2019 # '''Announcing [[MW:Talk:EMWCon Spring 2020|EMWCon 2020]]''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} I have full support of my management #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Would like to determine an organizing committee. Who is in-charge of the process? #* {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} We should define the process (it doesn't currently exist), but we would like to help where we can #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Noted, I just don't want to do anything out of normal practices #* {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Gave some background on NASA with regards to the conference and a possible tour #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} NASA is spread into 10 field centers #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} NASA Glen in Cleveland Ohio is lesser known. Most others are "mission" oriented, further north facilities are "tech/research" divisions #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} NASA Plum Brook Station is located in rural Ohio, "we are a torture chamber for equipment that is launched". Others design equipment, we reproduce flight/operation conditions #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We could do a tour including the world's largest space vacuum chamber #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We can offer conference facilities at no cost #** {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Are Foreign Nationals OK? #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Great question. We can either host within NASA, but would need prior notice for admitting foreign nationals or host at the [https://www.kalaharimeetings.com/ohio Kalahari conference center] (literally across the street) which would not need any prior notice. What are we trying to prioritize? 1) Cost or 2) Non-US attendance? #** {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} We have the budget from when we hosted in Virginia @ MITRE and we had foreign nationals which came with some restrictions, but we were able to accommodate #** {{Agenda presenter|Brian}} If the location requires early foreign national registration, it should be advertised early & clearly #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We would need to know the Min/Max attendees to contact Kalahari, do we know that? #** {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Min/Max is probably around 30-80, but it probably won't exceed 50 #** {{Agenda presenter|Gergo}} If you advertise the tour of NASA, we could get 100+ attendees, some of which have never used MW :) #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We should try to optimize "Maximum Pull", try to get the most people able to come. In Paris, 2 people added in the last 24 hours #** {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} Europeans will likely need to plan in advance anyway to just make the flight, usually 4 weeks #** {{Agenda presenter|Brian}} As a Canadian, we book at least 4 weeks due to cost. Also, Early access to program content is always a good idea
