". Others design equipment, we reproduce flight/operation conditions #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We could do a tour including the world's largest space vacuum chamber #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We can offer conference facilities at no cost #** {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Are Foreign Nationals OK? #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} Great question. We can either host within NASA, but would need prior notice for admitting foreign nationals or host at the [https://www.kalaharimeetings.com/ohio Kalahari conference center] (literally across the street) which would not need any prior notice. What are we trying to prioritize? 1) Cost or 2) Non-US attendance? #** {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} We have the budget from when we hosted in Virginia @ MITRE and we had foreign nationals which came with some restrictions, but we were able to accommodate #** {{Agenda presenter|Brian}} If the location requires early foreign national registration, it should be advertised early & clearly #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We would need to know the Min/Max attendees to contact Kalahari, do we know that? #** {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Min/Max is probably around 30-80, but it probably won't exceed 50 #** {{Agenda presenter|Gergo}} If you advertise the tour of NASA, we could get 100+ attendees, some of which have never used MW :) #** {{Agenda presenter|Rich Evans}} We should try to optimize "Maximum Pull", try to get the most people able to come. In Paris, 2 people added in the last 24 hours #** {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} Europeans will likely need to plan in advance anyway to just make the flight, usually 4 weeks #** {{Agenda presenter|Brian}} As a Canadian, we book at least 4 weeks due to cost. Also, Early access to program content is always a good idea # '''News channel for MW''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Richard}} As a group we need a place where news about MW, SMW, extensions, skins, etc. can be published #* {{Agenda presenter|Richard}} Technically it's planned to be supported by [https://en.hallowelt.com/ Hallo Welt!], but under the umbrella of MWStake #* {{Agenda presenter|Richard}} We'd like to start within the year #* {{Agenda presenter|Richard}} Any ideas for content? #* {{Agenda presenter|Richard}} Trying to address the needs not met by existing mailing lists, chat room, etc.
# '''Sunflower distribution''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Richard}} Pitched the idea for a "standard distribution of MediaWiki+ that all in the community could support and use #* {{Agenda presenter|Greg}} How would this distribution be used? I've been using Meza. Once VE or Elastic Search is included, it gets difficult #* {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Good point, we may have too many "brands" (MediaWiki, Semantic MediaWiki, BlueSpice, Meza, QualityBox, etc.) #* {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} Ideally we can define a "common core" that can be maintained by many people #* {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} This sounds like we are trying to find a consensus between different groups and users, how will we achieve this consensus? #** {{Agenda presenter|Greg}} We could use my [https://discourse.equality-tech.com Discourse Forum] or a wiki #* {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} I propose a governing document to clearly define what is included in the sunflower distribution, but others can imliment/orchestrate via Docker/Ansible/Kubernetes/etc. on CentOS/Debian/Ubuntu/etc. as they see fit. The document just defines the components.
