==Notes== # '''Meeting timing''' #* Some confusion over the meeting timing. #* (Georgios) UTC 15:30 (7:30am PST, 10:30am EST, 4:30pm CET) works best for Australian users. #* The UTC time was keep standard but the US daylight saving time change caused low meeting turn-out. In the future, keeping the same time in the US seems preferred. #* We need to work on a better communication method. Cindy, Rich, and Bryan to work together on improving communication. # '''(Markus) [[meta:Wikimedia Summit 2020|Wikimedia Summit]]''' #* Markus is planning on going as long as nobody else has any issue. #* The Summit dates conflict with [[MW:EMWCon Spring 2020|EMWCon 2020]] #** Better for carbon footprint if someone from Europe attends the Summit #* Markus requested inputs for agenda items he can bring to the Summit #* (Gergo) I might be there in some capacity as well # '''(Markus) MWStake Annual Reporting''' #* We need to create a list of "things we did" in [[mw:MediaWiki Stakeholders' Group/Annual Report 2019|2019]] similar to previous years ([[mw:MediaWiki Stakeholders' Group/Annual Report 2018|2018]]): #* As we formalize, we need to document our financing # '''(Rich) [[MW:EMWCon Spring 2020|EMWCon 2020]]''' #* Yaron agreed to front the money #* Contract with Kalahari Conference Center is being finalized and hopefully will be signed later today #* Please wait for the conference code to be announced to get the conference rates #* Who can help with taking on the role of a Chair? Cindy said her arm could be twisted. # Brian Wolff is back at the WMF and discussed his new role and some security related topics #* Content Security Policy (CSP) lets websites determine who they talk to #** Prevents Cross-site Scripting #** (Markus) How does the CSP support policy work? #*** (Brian) Typical usecase - Prevent Google Analytics, prevents inline Javascript, limits Cross-site Scripting # '''PageFoms Discussion''' #* Based on [[Wikiversity:WikiJournal User Group|WikiJournals]] recent [[meta:Community Wishlist Survey 2020/Wikiversity/Simple structured input forms|request]] for using PageForms from their [[meta:WikiJournal/Technical_wishlist|Technical Wishlist]] #* (Brian) Some things that would help get PageForms accepted by the WMF #** Important to align with WMF's code policy #** Adding Unit Tests #** Get internal Champion #** Could English Wikipedia add it to their Wishlist? They usually get what they ask for. #** Refactoring some of the most complex parts # '''(Gergo) Parsoid''' #* Used to be Node.js, now rewritten in PHP #* It's live now and seems to have decent performance benefits # '''(Gergo) Global Templates''' #* [[mw:Global templates/Proposed specification, short version|Proposed specification]]
