==Notes== # '''EMWCon pre-Pre-Conference''' #* (Cindy) Many people are coming in early (Sunday/Monday) to meet before #* (Cindy) Not formal, but we can discuss/meet/collaborate/hack/etc. #* (Lex) We can discuss fundraising #* (Bryan) We should have a group during the pre-conference (or maybe create camp during the conference) to discuss "Marketing MediaWiki" # '''[[MW:EMWCon Spring 2020|EMWCon 2020]] Update''' #* (Cindy) Venue reserved for "Pre-Conference" #* (Cindy) Conference rate ($104/night). Yaron is working to extend that to pre-conference attendees #* (Cindy) Cindy, Yaron, and Rich are meeting Wednesdays to continue planning #* (Cindy) Conference rate includes waterpark admission #* (Cindy) Sam Willson (WMF) will be arriving 1 day early #* (Daren) Does the room give access to your entire "group/family"? #** (Update) Each room is allotted 4 waterpark passes #* (Cindy) Conference dinner in Sandusky. We might need some travel coordination. #* (Cindy) We have arranged for video/live streaming #* (Cindy) We need notice in advance: #** 1 month - Foreign nationals #** 2 weeks - T-shirt sizing #* (Cindy) Only 1 talk so far has been announced, we need more #* (Cindy) At this point, it looks like a larger conference than normal (≈50 vs <45) #* (Ike) I'm arriving Tuesday, can provide rides for people #* (Bryan) I'm arriving Sunday evening and can provide rides (already have Lex and possibly Daren). Might be able to make a second trip. #* Should we discuss "wanted talks" for the conference? # '''WikiWho/WhoColor/WhoVIS demonstration''' #* (Bryan) Showed the browser extensions via example and some more analytics, see links above
# '''NEO4J''' #* (Lex) Has anyone dealt with [https://neo4j.com/ NEO4J] using semantic databases? #* (Lex) I'm using the [https://golang.org/ GO language] to query SMW via API # '''AlternativeTo.net''' #* (Lex) showed the group [https://alternativeto.net/ AlternativeTo.net], a crowdsourced website that lets you see alternative software choices #* (Daren) Why isn't MediaWiki shown as an alternative to SharePoint [https://alternativeto.net/software/microsoft-sharepoint/ on the site]? #* (Bryan) I added it, if people have time, create an account and vote for the same. Easiest way is to create an account, go to the [https://alternativeto.net/software/microsoft-sharepoint/ SharePoint] page, click the edit button (next to the Facebook and Twitter link) and "Add an alternative" # '''OrientDB.com''' #* (Lex) Another graph database I've looked into is [https://orientdb.com/ OrientDB]
