==Meeting agenda== # '''Wait for attendees & chat''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} # '''Wiki Quickie''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} #* [[URL highlighting text tinkering]] # '''MediaWiki Blog Released''' {{Agenda time|15 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Richard H}} #* https://mediawiki.blog #* Needs input: Authors, Corrections, Suggestions, etc. # '''This month in MediaWiki''' {{Agenda time|15 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Mark A. Hershberger}} # '''Agenda Item''' {{Agenda time|XX min}} {{Agenda presenter|TBD}} # '''Wiki Watercooler''' {{Agenda time|remaining}} {{Agenda presenter|Open Mic}}
==Notes== # '''What's new in MediaWiki''' (Cindy) discussed what's coming in MediaWiki based off the [https://etherpad.wikimedia.org/p/mwstake-2020-07 notes] prepared by Gergo #* 1.35 (out in a few weeks) will be the last release to support Internet Explorer (T248061) #* Uncached VisualEditor w/ Parsoid/PHP (no JS, no RESTBase) for MW 1.35 LTS (T248343) #* SkinTemplateOutputPageBeforeExec and a number of other hooks are being deprecated (T60137). #** See https://lists.wikimedia.org/pipermail/wikitech-l/2020-June/093556.html #** See https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/User:Jdlrobson/Skins_for_extension_developers #* Extensions can now provide alternative database backends (instead of the core MySQL, Postgres etc): https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T226857 #* Gerrit updated to version 3. You can now create and edit patches via the web interface. #** But apparently it will be replaced by GitLab next year: https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Release_Engineering_Team/GitLab #** GitLab is like a github, hosted elsewhere, e.g. WMF. It probably necessitates a switch from Jenkins to Argo. #* (Peter) Is it extraordinarily difficult to support IE? I'm surprised. In the fed govt many of us are supposed to use IE for some things and Edge has been unusable I'm told # '''MediaWiki Logo change proposal''' #* https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Project:Proposal_for_changing_logo_of_MediaWiki,_2020 # '''Wikimedia re-branding''' #* Survey and open letter from community #** https://wikimedia.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_9G2dN7P0T7gPqpD #** https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Community_open_letter_on_renaming #* Law of Triviality https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_of_triviality #* (Peter) I reviewed it and asked to hold until more information was captured # '''Abstract Wikipedia''' #* Approved by the Wikimedia Foundation Board of Trustee and Denny Vrandečić is joining the Foundation #* It looks like this will be a place to put Wikipedia pages that automatically translate into many languages. The pages will have some kind of sentences that refer to Wikidata items. #* (Mark) It may be too ambitious #** https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Abstract_Wikipedia/July_2020_announcement (Announcement) #** https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikilambda (Info) #** https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.04733 (White Paper) #** https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=23714875 (Hacker News with some commentary) # '''Page Exchange''' #* (Ike) Explained the extension use and development #* https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:Page_Exchange #* (Cindy) Does PageExchange resolve https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T177496? # '''MediaWiki blog''' #* (Richard) MediaWiki blog will be at https://mediawiki.blog (password protected) #* (Richard) The blog is ready to go but needs some help and final decision over the domain (mediawiki.blog) #* (Richard) Areas help is requested: #** Articles #** Expand "What's New" #** "About us", for example a page on MWStake #** Privacy law acceptable? It's written based on GDPR #*** (Bryan) If it's based on GDPR, it's likely ok for the rest of the world #* Should Board Members have their affiliation listed? (i.e. Board member X works for company Y) #* Will need articles - focused on mediawiki development? not enterprise wikis it seems
