{{Event |mwstake-meeting=No |title=Board Meeting |start-date=2020/06/05 |start-hour=14 |start-minute=00 |end-date=2020/06/05 |end-hour=15 |end-minute=00 |attendees=Bryan Hildebrand, Cindy Cicalese, Eric-Jan, James Montalvo, Lex Sulzer, Mark Hershberger }} ==Meeting agenda== # '''Sales Deck Presentation''' - [[Sales deck]] # '''Membership Guaranteed Projects''' - [[Dues]]
==Notes== The meeting voice transcription is available on the [[Event_talk:{{PAGENAME}}|talk page]]. # '''Sales Deck Presentation''' - [[Sales deck]] #* (Eric-Jan) Presented the [[Sales deck/Sales Deck Construction|Deck]] #* (Bryan) The goal of the deck is to have it used in conjunction with one of us reaching out to a potential sponsor, not a stand-alone "mailer" #* (Lex) Wikipedia has ideological goal, a path that people can connect to, so donating to Wikipedia aligns with that. What is our ideological goal? Passion? #* (Lex) With regards to my clients, the goal should be tied to something more practical. #* (James) I'd like to bring this to my management to get this group off the ground, this group represents our use case. Giving us money will help with the "Chicken-and-Egg" problem. You can be a sponsor & "Founding Member" to get some good name recognition for the sponsoring company. #* (Cindy) "Your Wiki - Our Passion" gives me the impression we are contractors, i.e. we will take your money and give you support. We aren't contractors, we are a community, support sounds commercial, passion should like "let's hold hands and sing Kumbaya" # '''Next meeting''' #* A vote was called to have another meeting in 2 weeks (June 19th, 1.5 hours earlier than normal) #** Vote was unanimously approved #* {{Action}} Schedule meeting # '''Membership Guaranteed Projects''' - [[Dues]] #* (Lex) I would like to use MWStake to provide a security review for pay (my Gold/Platinum membership) #* (Lex) I reached out to Brian Wolff, but he now works for Asana #* (Cindy) Sam Wilson might be a good fit
==Actions== {{Actionable board |Open |{{PAGENAME}} |MWStake |True |View |{{PAGENAME}} }}

{{Event |mwstake-meeting=No |title=Board Meeting |start-date=2020/06/19 |start-hour=12 |start-minute=30 |end-date=2020/06/19 |end-hour=13 |end-minute=30 |attendees=Bryan Hildebrand, Cindy Cicalese, Eric-Jan, James Montalvo, Lex Sulzer, Mark Hershberger, Markus Glaser }} ==Notes== The meeting voice transcription is available on the [[Event_talk:{{PAGENAME}}|talk page]]. # '''Credit Card Processing''' #* (Mark) We decided to use Wikibase to implement the Credit Card Processing (through Authorize.net) #** A vote was called #*** Vote was unanimously approved # '''[https://mediawiki.blog/ MediaWiki blog]'''
Status of CC processing (Agreed to use Wikibase to do it at $90/hr, Eric-Jan to report) Status of plan for brokerage (Lex's initial work here: MWStake Development Work Brokerage) Status of blog & trademark issue (Markus to report)
==Actions== {{Actionable board |Open |{{PAGENAME}} |MWStake |True |View |{{PAGENAME}} }}

{{Event |mwstake-meeting=No |title=Board Meeting |start-date=2020/06/19 |start-hour=12 |start-minute=30 |end-date=2020/06/19 |end-hour=13 |end-minute=30 |attendees=Bryan Hildebrand, Cindy Cicalese, Eric-Jan, James Montalvo, Lex Sulzer, Mark Hershberger, Markus Glaser }} ==Notes== The meeting voice transcription is available on the [[Event_talk:{{PAGENAME}}|talk page]]. # '''Credit Card Processing''' #* (Mark) {{Action}} We decided to implement the Credit Card Processing (through Authorize.net) using Wikibase $90/hr, Eric-Jan to report #* A vote was called to have Wikibase handle the development work to implement Credit Card Processing #** Vote was unanimously approved
# '''[https://mediawiki.blog/ MediaWiki blog]''' #* In previous converstation, Gergo brought up possible trademark issues #* Ideally we can get permission to use the URL (mediawiki.blog) from the WMF to operate the blog #* We should transfer the URL to MWStake from Hallo Welt #* {{Action}} (Markus) To approach the WMF about operating the blog and transferring the domain to MWStake #* {{Action}} (Mark) Actually, I need to transfer the mwstake.org domain to MWStake as well since I currently own it #* (Cindy) I talked to Chris Koerner, he said talk to WMF Trademarks to ensure it is OK #* (Markus) Wikimedia.de is owned by Wikimedia Germany, not WMF, so there is good history #* {{Action}} (Markus) We should have AFCom (Affiliates Committee) review our [[Bylaws]] #* A vote was called to have Markus talk to AFCom about our Bylaws, talk to WMF Trademarks about operating the blog, and transferring the domain (mediawiki.blog) to MWStake #** Vote was unanimously approved # '''First MWStake Project''' #* (Mark) The subcommittee (Cindy, Mark, Evita) were tasked to find a "First Project" for MWStake #* (Mark) Goal was to find a project that can be completed in 6 months #* (Mark) Be able to point to it as a "we did this" with a success #* (Mark) The PDF rendering extension, [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:Collection Collection], used to be very useful but has broken #* (Mark) We have found the extension [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:DocBookExport DocBookExport] which can print multiple pages #* (Mark) The goal is to use DocBookExport as the backend to fix Collection #* (Cindy) There is a crucial first step requried, secure the money to pay a developer # '''MWStake project brokerage''' #* (Lex) With respect to my email (regarding paid work for security review), we need to get the project execution capability of MWStake established #* (Mark) Sounds like we (MWStake) are more like "brokers" vs. "consultants" #* (Lex) Yes, like an "escrow" service #* (Markus) Code review is an area we might really be of service #* (Mark) A subcommittee is needed for the for the "scoping, intake, and hand-off" of projects for guaranteed sponsorship projects where we (MWStake) act as project brokers #* (Cindy) We need to have a description of the process, then use an example project like Lex's #* {{Action}} Lex and Eric-Jan to collaborate on a process to intake and execute on this activity #** (Lex) My initial draft is [https://manage.mwstake.org/wiki/C0398617288# here] (request access from Lex if you don't already have it) # '''Sales Slide Deck''' #* Are we ready to give someone at a company/organization enough "ammo" to "sell" an MWStake sponsorship to their management"? If not, what is needed?
==Actions== {{Actionable board |Open |{{PAGENAME}} |MWStake |True |View |{{PAGENAME}} }}

