{{Event |mwstake-meeting=Yes |start-date=2020/09/04 |start-hour=15 |start-minute=30 |end-date=2020/09/04 |end-hour=16 |end-minute=30 |url=https://meet.google.com/mdd-ufhn-ksb |attendees=Brian Wolff, Bryan Hildebrand, Evita Hollis, Lex Sulzer, Mark Hershberger, Peter Meyer, Vincent Brooks }} ==Meeting agenda== # '''Wait for attendees & chat''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} # <del>'''Wiki Quickie''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} {{Agenda presenter|TBD}}</del> # <del>'''MediaWiki Blog Released''' {{Agenda time|15 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Richard H}}</del> #* <del>https://mediawiki.blog</del> #* <del>Needs input: Authors, Corrections, Suggestions, etc.</del> # '''MediaWiki News''' {{Agenda time|20 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} # '''Wiki Watercooler''' {{Agenda time|remaining}} {{Agenda presenter|Open Mic}}
==Notes== The meeting voice transcription is available on the [[Event_talk:{{PAGENAME}}|talk page]]. # '''Help Desk''' #* (Mark) Thanked Brian Wolff for his support desk help # '''This month in MediaWiki''' (Mark) - Based off [https://etherpad.wikimedia.org/p/mwstake-2020-09 Etherpad notes] #* MW Logo Change #** One week left to comment on the [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Project:Proposal_for_changing_logo_of_mediawiki,_2020 MW Logo change] #* The deprecation policy discussion. https://lists.wikimedia.org/pipermail/wikitech-l/2020-August/093761.html #* MW 1.35 release candidate. (VE in core!) #** @tgr says this means no external dependencies for DiscussionTools https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:DiscussionTools #* Updated pingback statistics visualization using the heartbeat ping: https://pingback.wmflabs.org/#media-wiki-version. A chart is shown. The data show how relatively common MediaWiki 1.30 to 1.35 are, and new installations of each #* https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Developer_Advocacy/Developer_Portal #* PHP 7.2 support is dropped for MW 1.35, https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T257879 #* the discussion about unsupporting single-step upgrades over lots of versions is still ongoing, #* there is a consultation about switching from Gerrit to Gitlab. https://lists.wikimedia.org/pipermail/wikitech-l/2020-September/093816.html #* Plus the MediaWiki user survey https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/2020_MediaWiki_User_Survey #* A discussion for the Wikimedia Universal Code of Conduct is coming up. I imagine it will replace the CoC for technical spaces (although no one explicitly stated that) so somewhat relevant for non-#* Wikimedians as well. https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Universal_Code_of_Conduct #* What happened with MagicNumberedHeadings and why you should keep mw.or up-to-date #** MNH initially stored code in the page on mw.o #** When I went to update it, I learned Umherirrender had imported MagicNumberedHeadings from my github repo into gerrit but neither he nor I updated MW.o to point to the repo(s) instead of having code on the page, so @kghbln looked at the page and said, hmm, not updated for MagicWords and MWServices (but I did this on my github repo and @legoktm did it on gerrit) #** So, @kghbln marked the extension archived and, as a result, Archive the MagicNumberedHeadings extension (https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T248758) archived the gerrit repo. #** I was upgrading and noticed all this. Asked for a gerrit repo re-creation. # '''New Flex Diagrams extension''' #* [[MW:Extension:Flex Diagrams|Flex Diagrams]] extension from Yaron #* Offers support for BPMN, Gantt, and Mermaid. Editable examples below: #** [https://discoursedb.org/w/index.php?title=BPMN:Hi&action=editdiagram BPMN] #** [https://discoursedb.org/w/index.php?title=Gantt:Project_ATLAS&action=editdiagram Gantt] #** [https://discoursedb.org/w/index.php?title=Mermaid:Sample_diagram&action=editdiagram Mermaid]
==Action board== {{Actionable board |Open |{{PAGENAME}} |MWStake |True |View |{{PAGENAME}} }}

