{{Event |mwstake-meeting=Yes |start-date=2020/10/02 |start-hour=15 |start-minute=30 |end-date=2020/10/02 |end-hour=16 |end-minute=30 |url=https://meet.google.com/mdd-ufhn-ksb |attendees=Bernhard Krabina, Bryan Hildebrand, Cindy Cicalese, Evita Hollis, Ike Hecht, Lex Sulzer, Mark Hershberger, Markus Glaser, Megan Cutrofello, Richard Heigl, Sam Nguyen }} ==Meeting agenda== # '''Wait for attendees & chat''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} # '''Wiki Quickie''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} {{Agenda presenter|TBD}} # '''MediaWiki News''' {{Agenda time|20 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} # '''[[mw:Extension:StructuredNavigation|StructuredNavigation]]''' {{Agenda time|20 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Samantha}} # '''Movement Strategy Discussions''' {{Agenda time|15 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Gergo}} or {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} #* Should MWStake help with [https://www.mediawiki.org/w/index.php?title=Topic:Vunb24jox2rjf2o5 organizing movement strategy discussions]? # '''Wiki Watercooler''' {{Agenda time|remaining}} {{Agenda presenter|Open Mic}}
==Notes== The meeting voice transcription is available on the [[Event_talk:{{PAGENAME}}|talk page]]. # '''What's new in MW''' ([https://etherpad.wikimedia.org/p/mwstake-2020-10 Etherpad]) #* [https://lists.wikimedia.org/pipermail/wikitech-l/2020-September/093827.html Extension Developer RFC] - Parsoid & Extensions #* [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Universal_Code_of_Conduct/Draft_review New Code of Conduct] #* [https://lists.wikimedia.org/pipermail/mediawiki-l/2020-September/048471.html Looking] for a maintainer for the [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:Lingo Lingo Extension] #* [https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSc5tGeRixL62mT90TwRGTtQXq-MeN6jUcBnCwKqmBo_lzXOyQ/viewform PHP Community Survey] #* [https://www.semantic-mediawiki.org/wiki/SMWCon_Fall_2020 SMWCon 2020] #* [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Project:Proposal_for_changing_logo_of_MediaWiki,_2020/Round_2 MediaWiki logo change] - Now at round 2 # '''GitLab consultation''' #* [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Talk:GitLab_consultation Discussion on mediawiki.org] #* {{Agenda presenter|Sam}} liked the UI for Gerrit #* {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} I'm on the GitLab consultation group #** The community (MW) wasn't happy about the speed/notice about the decision to switch, but it does seem like it's happening #** Only if the council '''really''' disapproves will it be blocked. #** The council is comprised of 10 people, 7 of which are on the WMF. #** The case has to be strong to prevent moving forward #** (Cindy) Some outside & within the Foundation liked some of Gerrit's features #** Since the WMF would become a strategic partner and a high notoriety one, we can push for the opensourcing of some features of GitLab which would be a community win # '''WikiMedia Strategy Recommendation''' - [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Strategy/Wikimedia_movement/2018-20/Recommendations#Want_to_experience_this_content_in_another_format? Overview] #* Gergo pointed this out #* {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} I'm interested in helping here. I see two areas we can be involved: #*# [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Strategy/Wikimedia_movement/2018-20/Recommendations/Improve_User_Experience User Experience] - Changes here effect all of us. At the least knowing what's coming and proactively helping guide changes to benefit our community. #*# [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Strategy/Wikimedia_movement/2018-20/Recommendations/Manage_Internal_Knowledge Manage Internal Knowledge] - Many of us have a lot of experience documenting processes and capturing tribal knowledge, this is an area I can "give back" to MediaWiki # '''StructuredNavigation''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Sam Nguyen}} presented her new extension [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:StructuredNavigation StructuredNavigation] #* (HOLD for slide deck) #* {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} Offered a suggestion to allow "red links" to work with the extension based on [[MW:Manual:$wgRegisterInternalExternals]] # '''MediaWiki Blog''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Richard}} The blog is now live here: [https://mediawikiexperts.blog/ mediawikiexperts.blog] #* {{Agenda presenter|Richard}} Suggested that Sam could write something (possibly on StructuredNavigation)
