{{Event |mwstake-meeting=Yes |start-date=2020/12/04 |start-hour=16 |start-minute=30 |end-date=2020/12/04 |end-hour=17 |end-minute=30 |url=https://meet.google.com/mdd-ufhn-ksb |attendees=Bernhard Krabina, Bryan Hildebrand, Cindy Cicalese, Gergő Tisza, Ike Hecht, Jeroen De Dauw, Lex Sulzer, Mark Hershberger, Markus Glaser, Peter Meyer, Peter Woudsma, Rich Evans, Vincent Brooks, Yaron Koren, Geert Van Pamel, Tim Ruijters, Caleb Cooper, Alex Tanchoco, Igor Absorto, Lexi McGillivray, Michael Barylak, Bob Watts, Nick Parrott, Patrick Marvin }} ==Meeting agenda== # '''Wait for attendees & chat''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} # '''MediaWiki News''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} # '''SMWCon''' {{Agenda time|20 min}} {{Agenda presenter|TBD}} #* The [https://www.semantic-mediawiki.org/wiki/SMWCon_Fall_2020 Semantic MediaWiki Conference] this year was a huge success #* Some discussions about what worked well and any issues that came up #* [https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLw2YgbWET_pgT_oUsampBL8O6osinnNW8 YouTube Playlist] # '''[https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Community_Wishlist_Survey_2021 Community Wishlist Survey 2021]''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} #* The submission phase is now closed (30NOV) with 288 proposals #* The voting phase is coming up (08DEC – 21DEC) #* Any feedback is welcome, some things I found interesting that might be relevant to MWStake: #** [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Community_Wishlist_Survey_2021/Editing#Copy_and_paste_from_diffs Copy and paste from diffs] (Editing) #** [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Community_Wishlist_Survey_2021/Miscellaneous#Bring_back_PDF_book_rendering Bring back PDF book rendering] (Misc.) #** [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Community_Wishlist_Survey_2021/Multimedia_and_Commons#Support_360_photo_viewing Support 360 photo viewing] (Multimedia & Commons) #** [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Community_Wishlist_Survey_2021/Wikidata Section on Wikidata] # '''WMF Stable Interface Policy''' {{Agenda time|10 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} #* The email from WMF mentions MWStake #* https://lists.wikimedia.org/pipermail/wikitech-l/2020-December/094086.html #* https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T268328 #* https://github.com/MWStake/nonwmf-extensions # '''Creating reusable MediaWiki products''' {{Agenda time|15 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}} #* Developing community driven MediaWiki products (ISO, CRM, BPM, etc.) that can be shared via [[MW:Extension:Page Exchange|Page Exchange]]/Docker # '''How to become a member''' {{Agenda time|5 min}} {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} #* Information about how to become an MWStake member # '''Wiki Watercooler''' {{Agenda time|remaining}} {{Agenda presenter|Open Mic}}
==Notes== # '''MediaWiki News''' {{Agenda presenter|Gergo}} #* Proposal to make shelling out from MediaWiki containerizable: https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T260330 #* Firefox required version upped to 3.6: https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T262946 #* A bunch more requirement changes are being discussed: https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T266866 #* RfC for a more formalized way to provide config snippets, mainly for testing: https://phabricator.wikimedia.org/T267928 #* Old RfCs still being discussed: extension Composer compatibility, DB upgrade support for old versions #* Wikimedia Movement Strategy Global Conversations: https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Strategy/Wikimedia_movement/2018-20/Transition/Global_Conversations # '''SMWCon''' {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} #* [https://www.semantic-mediawiki.org/wiki/SMWCon_Fall_2020 SMWCon Page] #* Many thanks to Bernhard Krabina, Richard Heigl, and others that put it together, it was a great success #* Some statistics: #** '''234''' - Registered #** '''92''' - Max concurrent at event #** '''74''' - Max concurrent during an individual session #* Not all the talks are out yet, but here is the [https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLw2YgbWET_pgT_oUsampBL8O6osinnNW8 YouTube playlist] #* Wikidata was a big topic during the conference with several topics devoted to it #* The [https://hopin.com/ hop.in] platform was very nice and added a lot of "conference like" features # '''Community Wishlist Survey 2021''' #* [https://meta.wikimedia.org/wiki/Community_Wishlist_Survey_2021 link to survey] # '''WMF Stable Interface Policy''' # '''Creating reusable MediaWiki products''' # '''How to become a member''' # '''WikiConference North America (WCNA) # '''Chat service recommendation'''
