Meeting notes for '''MediaWiki "Products" Discussion''' (Fri Dec 18 16:00-17:00 UTC 2020)
<div style="float:right; border:1px solid black; padding:5px; margin-bottom:15px; border-radius:5px; background-color:#b3e0ff; "> <span style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:underline;">Attendees</span>
* Ad Strack van Schijndel
* Bryan Hilderbrand
* Eric-Jan van Kakerken
* Greg Rundlett
* Ike Hecht
* Lex Sulzer
* Lexi McGillivray
* Markus Glaser
* Rich Evans
* Richard Heigl
* Yaron Koren
</div>

# Introductions
# {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}
#* 30s Elevator Pitch
# {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}
#* Does this represent a way to pay for things? (buy a fix for an issue, etc.)
#* What is the governance model?
# {{Agenda presenter|Markus}}
#* Like a common core?  Or a collection of Use Cases (Templates + Use Cases)?
#** Each product would be MW + Extensions + Templates/Forms {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}
#* MWStake already exists, should this be under their umbrella?
#** Could be.  Or [https://www.opensemanticdata.org/ Open Semantic Data Association] (OSDA) {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}
# {{Agenda presenter|Ad}}
#* This is similar to the talk I gave at SMWCon2020 called "MediaWiki based open source content services platform"''' ([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hMHcO9AG7ww YouTube link])
#* We need a "common foundation" (MW + Extensions + Search + etc.)
#* Internally we have a tool to "sync" via git
#* We have CRM & Workflow modules
#* Could have a menu with a dropdown so people can add other "Products"/"Components"/"Modules"
#** I think it's better to sell each thing as a stand-alone Product without overselling it as something that "does everything".  Better to undersell & then grow {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}
# {{Agenda presenter|Richard}}
#* We need a distribution of MW+
#* Something like the "Sunflower Distribution" (discussed during an MWStake meeting on 04OCT19 [https://mwstake.org/mwstake/wiki/Event:93 link])
# {{Agenda presenter|Eric-Jan}}
#* "Content Services Suite"
# {{Agenda presenter|Ad}}
#* I think we should focus on the platform with one approach
#** We can do that in parallel {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}
# {{Agenda presenter|Lex}}
#* Should we start with concept vs. technical first?
#** End Users
#** Admins
#** Customers' Developers
#**: [[File:Concept vs Technical.png|border|400px]]
# {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}
#* We have a solution for MW+, Meza!
#* Software Version Description
#** Known set of software that plays well together
#** Use git
#* Different approach from Software <--> Templates/Forms/etc.
#** Doesn't use git
#** Need to bring wiki content under version control (like git)
#*** Totally agree {{Agenda presenter|Ad}}
#*** Could store it on git {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}
#* {{Agenda presenter|Eric-Jan}}
#** Draw up a list of standard products Ad & Yaron agree on
# {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}
#* Document Management is a good package idea
#* I've been working on a solution and have it deployed on my wikis
# {{Agenda presenter|Richard}}
#* Need to define a list of requirements
#** Requirements are at the core of my world {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}
#** Good requirements just mean, "I provide this"
# {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}
#* ISO seems like a good "product"
#** Yes, this is a good Use Case {{Agenda presenter|Richard}}
# {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}}
#* Are/Should "Help Pages" shipped with the products
#* Having good documentation/manual really helps with adoption
# {{Agenda presenter|Ad}}
#* We have a "People"/"Organization" Product
#** Would you be willing to "open source" it? {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}
#*** We would consider it {{Agenda presenter|Ad}}
# {{Agenda presenter|Eric-Jan}}
#* All this is high level/technical, we need the marketing approach
#** Mission/Vision/Values {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}
#** Clearly we have interest/traction {{Agenda presenter|Yaron}}

