{{Event |mwstake-meeting=No |title=Board Meeting |start-date=2021/01/28 |start-hour=03 |start-minute=30 |end-date=2021/01/28 |end-hour=04 |end-minute=30 |attendees=Bernhard Krabina, Bryan Hildebrand, Cindy Cicalese, Eric-Jan, Evita Hollis, Lex Sulzer, Mark Hershberger, Markus Glaser }} ==Agenda== From the [[Event:131|minutes of the last meeting]]. We need to flesh out the areas of activity for 2021: # MWStake.org and WikiApiary.org hosting # Code of Conduct # MWStake Membership #* Credit Card processing for all options (individual, corporate, donations, conference tickets, etc.) #* Acquiring new members #* Acquiring new sponsors
==Notes== The meeting voice transcription is available on the [[Event_talk:{{PAGENAME}}|talk page]]. # '''Welcome Bernhard as the newest Board Member''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} What are some problems you want to solve? #* {{Agenda presenter|Bernhard}} I'd live to solve the SMW development issue #* {{Agenda presenter|Bernhard}} First the compatibility with MW 1.35 #** {{Agenda presenter|Bernhard}} SMW is already compatible, however other extensions aren't. For example Semantic Glossary. #* {{Agenda presenter|Bernhard}} We need a process for testing (extensions) and a list of "watched/tracked" extensions #* {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} What about recording problems/tracking bugs? Is that just done on extension talk pages? #* {{Agenda presenter|Bernhard}} Yeah, that's a problem #* {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} Yes, I share your concern, especially with upcoming changes to core #* {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} Jeroen does not have the time to take on full scale support of SMW, but there is definitely a need #* {{Agenda presenter|Eric}}We have a forked version of Semantic Glossary on 1.35 and we can share #* {{Agenda presenter|Bernhard}} That's actually part of the problem, there are lots of people/companies with fixes, but not submitting PR to fix the codebase # '''Code of Conduct''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Evita}} I put the [[Code of conduct]] in MWStake #* {{Agenda presenter|Evita}} We need to discuss how this is handled. The reporting person's identity should be anonymous #* {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} Should it be both secret (only a few people on a code of conduct committee or something should see it) and anonymous (not everyone or anyone? knows who the reporting person is)? #** {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} I think there would be a group that knows the person reporting but beyond that they remain anonymous #* {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} Sounds like we need to create a group. Should it be only Board Members, only Individual Members, or at least 1 Board Member? #** {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} Not all Board, there could be an issue with the Board #** {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Probably a few people. Not 10, more like 3 # '''[https://mwstake.org/mwstake/wiki/Main_Page MWStake.org] & [https://www.wikiapiary.com/wiki/Main_Page WikiApiary.com] hosting''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Mark}} Who can help? #* {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} & {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} can help #* {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} I have some AWS experience # '''Next meetings''' #* {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}} I'd like to talk about the "MWStake Machinery" (How Board Members are voted on in elections, Annual Meeting of Members, etc.) #** {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} We should discuss this in 2 weeks (after next weeks regular MWStake meeting) #* {{Agenda presenter|Markus}} There's the regular MWStake meeting next week #** {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}} We should publicize this again # '''Conference platform''' #* {{Action}} {{Agenda presenter|Bernhard}} I actually have a task I still need to do. Write-up my experience using [https://hopin.com/ HopIn] for [https://www.semantic-mediawiki.org/wiki/SMWCon_Fall_2020 SMWCon2020]
==Actions== {{Actionable board |All |{{PAGENAME}} |MWStake |True |View |{{PAGENAME}} }}

