ube.com/watch?v=dgCvpy2P_Fo&list=PLQVG_tuf3Q2c9MIMVeuoI8Q7eFrnT9Mdi&index=5 # {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}}: And, of course, Tom talking about PowerPedia at the same conference:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jfkfMHl4DQw&list=PLQVG_tuf3Q2c9MIMVeuoI8Q7eFrnT9Mdi&index=9 #* And, the full federal government panel: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vZQ6lWg5Hww&list=PLQVG_tuf3Q2c9MIMVeuoI8Q7eFrnT9Mdi&index=10 # {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}: I took Yaron's WikiWorks "one good knife" analogy and generalized it for MW in general .. here it is: https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Topic:Xjac81qdj0igo64t # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: https://www.cisa.gov/zero-trust-maturity-model # {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}}: https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/M-22-09.pdf # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: https://www.intelink.gov/ # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: Sorry to eat up so much meeting time # {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}}: No, that was really helpful, thanks Tom. #* I'd really like to know how we can help advocate for Powerpedia (using MW!). # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: Thank you! # {{Agenda presenter|Markus}}: Thanks Gergö # {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}}: I think that was you Rich! # {{Agenda presenter|Cindy}}: I still think we need the Acquia of MediaWiki: https://www.acquia.com/drupal/acquia-drupal # {{Agenda presenter|Bryan}}: While MediaWiki is not a single software element solution that checks all the boxes of a security plan by itself (nothing is), it can, when used in conjunction with other administrative and technical elements of an overall system, definitely serve as the core element of a very secure knowledge infrastructure implementation. ~ Rich Evans (date unknown) # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: Acquia does an excellent job of promoting Druapl. I would love to see the same for MediaWiki. # I feel like there are some efforts # {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}: NIST FIPS-199 defines 3 dimensions of cybersecurity: ## Confidentiality ## Integrity ## Accessibility # {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}: And each IT system is requires to rate each of these dimensions in one of 3 levels: ## LOW ## MODERATE ## HIGH # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: https://canasta.wiki/ or https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Meza? # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: Government wiki farm #* Plus adding some good starter templates (infobox, navbox, etc.) with template data # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: I would love to see NASA offer that as a service #* The CSP should be FedRAMP compliant # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: Rich - Could you share more details at an upcoming Federal meeting? # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: https://usalearning.gov/ hosts NRC wiki # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: Where is my ITIL manual when I need it # {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}: NIST FIPS 200 defines 20 control groups # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: https://wiki.en.it-processmaps.com/index.php/Availability_Management # {{Agenda presenter|Rich}}: NIST SP-800-53 Rev 5 # {{Agenda presenter|Tom}}: We will let our ISSO team read Rev 5 # {{Agenda presenter|Nick}}: please respond to jeff's email. i am curious what the team thinks.
