==Notes== * Rocky Linux is now basis for MEZA as a result ** what is Rocky Linux? *** RHEL is commericial branch *** CentOS is RHEL without subscription *** CentOS came to impasse *** Rocky Linux 8 — currently dust hasn't settled (another challenger to the CentOS throne) * Rich want's MEZA to be standard MW distribution ** Updated documentation to Meza * MEZA is officially NASA open source ** Switched to NASA repository ** Created a Common Meza Test Environment to provide a baseline. * Containerization ** Meza and canasta working together? * What about 1.39 is harder? Why only recently on 1.35? ** Major users of MEZA are on older versions (e.g. 1.31) and will update to 1.35 first. ** Want to wait until “all the popcorn is popped” before upgrading. * Information on MediaWiki usage inside NASA ** Internal “MediaWiki Stakeholder's” group ** Handbook that recommends MW (as well as Confluence) for Knowledge Management.
